<div class="sec" id="s10">
  <div class="num">10</div>
  <h2>Glossary</h2>
  <div class="kv">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">agent</div><p>
        An AI that can act, not only answer. Reads and edits files, runs
        commands, checks its own work.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">prompt</div><p>
        What you type to an AI. The better it is structured, the better the
        result.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">repository</div><p>
        A project folder with a Git save history attached. Often shortened to
        repo.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">terminal</div><p>
        A window where you type commands to the computer instead of clicking.
        Claude Code runs in one.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">commit</div><p>
        One saved snapshot of a project in Git. You can go back to any commit.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">Git</div><p>
        The tool that keeps that save history. Ask the agent to set it up; you
        rarely need to touch it directly.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">thread</div><p>
        In Delta, one task: the conversation with the agent plus the changes it
        made, kept together.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">editor</div><p>
        A program for opening and changing text files, which is what code is.
        Zed is one.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">ACP</div><p>
        Agent Client Protocol. A shared language that lets editors talk to
        agents. Why Zed can run Claude.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">CLAUDE.md</div><p>
        A text file in your project that Claude Code reads on every start. Your
        standing instructions.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">skill</div><p>
        A reusable pack of instructions you can call by name, like a recipe card
        for a job you do often.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="term">Jev</div><p>
        A model that picks a decision from a list instead of chatting. Fast and
        cheap for small repeated choices.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p style="color: var(--color-4f9a68); font-size: 15px; padding-top: 24px">
    Made for NZB. Check the live docs whenever a step looks different from what
    is written here.
  </p>
</div>
